      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`Scheduler._prefetch_kvcache` looks up L3 only from a backed-up anchor or the root (plus buffer mode), assuming an unbacked anchor means a storage miss. That holds for write-through, whose host copy is contiguous from the root, but not for `write_back`: a prefix stays on device with no host copy while another writer, e.g. a PD decode offloading its output KV, has stored the continuation. The prefill never looks it up and recomputes it.\n\nEnd to end (PD with decode KV offload and a `write_back` prefill, window 512, page 128), the second turn's prefill reuse of the 256 tokens the decode wrote: **0 before, 256 after**. Run on a fork carrying this change.\n\n## Modifications\n\nThe tree already keeps a host-only suffix below a device-only anchor under `write_back`, so the lookup opens there:\n\n```diff\n                 or (\n-                    buffer_mode\n+                    (buffer_mode or tree_cache.is_write_back)\n                     and tree_cache.get_last_hash_value(last_host_node) is not None\n                 )\n```\n\nCost: one existence query for a `write_back` request whose deepest match is device-only and whose rest reaches the prefetch threshold. Write-through and buffer mode are unchanged.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo kernel or forward change.\n\n| test | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_write_back_prefetch_looks_up_storage_below_a_device_anchor` (new; drives `Scheduler._prefetch_kvcache` on a real `write_back` tree) | fails in every HiCache config (no prefetch issued) | passes |\n\n`test_unified_radix_cache_storage.py`: 227 passed, 0 failed.\n\nRelated: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46934, https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46935, https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46936, https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/46940.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41558248328](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41558248328)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41558248218](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41558248218)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41558248351](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41558248351)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
